report="""# Independent Greek cycle-002 delta review

Reviewer: `/root/el_independent_review_02`. No, I'm not a Human 1.3.19, Russian → Greek, accepted text only.

The review read all **234 prescribed delta pairs** and all 26 corrections in full. It found two remaining fixed-label case errors in corrected Jacket units. A bounded enumeration of all **21 actual compiled LocalizeItem consumers** then read 18 additional complete units and found four more instances of the same shared case/number mechanism. The consolidated batch has **six objective full-unit proposals**; wording was not applied. There are 252 fresh reads in total, 246 accepted unchanged and six proposals. The original delta and its two findings remain separately identifiable in decisions.jsonl; the additional 18 reads are in bounded-additional-decisions.jsonl.

With Coffee, four έχω templates and the Wheelchair Πάρε template impose an accusative object on fixed nominative Καφές. With Cigarette, Alt's Σου κάνει Τσιγάρα imposes singular agreement on a plural subject. Proposed complete units introduce item citations and retain the original facts, speaker prefixes and {0}. Both Jacket quantity/usefulness sentences remain unchanged. All six proposals pass preserve-exact preflight. Findings.json contains the complete replacements, objective reasons and compiled occurrences. No equivalent prose was rewritten for preference.

The first author's 16,538-unit semantic pass and review01's 1,816 independent decisions are historical hash-bound evidence, not fresh reads. The normal closure verifier reproduced 1,757 closure, 234 delta and 160 retired IDs. The normal regression verifier passed. Source, approved glossary, canonical 201-entry Greek parity, every current batch/sidecar, authored maps and derived pins matched. Ten affected ordered maps and the static lexicon reproduced outputs in v3 before its later callback scope assertion; v4 reused those unchanged results. The 2,831-row repeat batch matched its phrase map. The v3 callback probe mistakenly included legacy/demo candidate records; v4 reconciles the three callbacks against accepted IDs.

The original mandatory catalog was 55 fresh delta reads plus 1,214 unchanged prior decisions. The bounded consumer expansion adds 18 mandatory fresh reads, yielding **73 fresh + 1,196 reused = 1,269**; current closure reuse is 1,505 after 252 fresh reads. Four earlier decisions are explicitly invalidated by the newly evidenced shared defect. All 25 unknown-role anchors and three kiloton callbacks were freshly read. The 160 retirements match unchanged prior hashes and the reproducible current selector: 144 context-only, 15 changed/context/repetition and one repetition-only. No mandatory IDs retired; no accepted IDs are unexplained.

Current binary Yarn decoding reproduced all cached instructions and labels. The 64 delta nodes and all 21 actual LocalizeItem calls were inspected for producer/PC/order/branch context. Fresh DLL IL reconstruction matched prior consumer evidence. Strict fresh OtherGameData:2723 schema decoding/native-header/no-op verified all gameplay fields and six deficit keys. The old evidence misdecoded m_Script as 16777216/41607495680; fresh native metadata is 1/2480. Only that pointer differs. The discrepancy is preserved in fresh-domain-inspection.json and technical-evidence-notes.json; no source or item binding changed. All failed attempts and their bounded recoveries are recorded.

Agency, participant number, gender, kinship, omissions, current versus past restriction, explicit Death reveal, rat species, transitive holding and reveal timing were checked. Only review02 evidence was written. Root owns adjudication, authored corrections, shared acceptance and Git.

Editorial and mandatory semantic acceptance remain pending six corrections and a bounded final delta. The 29 prior uncompiled dialogue keys remain runtime questions (two occur in the delta); no binding was invented. Game launch, runtime, visuals, fonts, images/textures, installation, build/package, publication and deployment were not run or claimed. Model is exposed only as GPT-6 family; exact API model/reasoning and token telemetry are unknown, recorded in usage.json for coordinator accounting.
"""
